{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_EM_02276","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_EM_02276@rel:R25-11#4f8bba6e","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_EM_02276","release":"R25-11","content":"function Create [SWS_EM_02276] Upstream: RS_EM_00101 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00144 , RS_AP_00159 static ara::core::Result &lt; StateClient &gt; Create ( std::function &lt; void(const ara::exec::ExecutionErrorEvent &amp;)&gt; undefinedStateCallback) noexcept; Named constructor for StateClient. Header-Datei #include \"ara/exec/state_client.h\" class mono Scope class ara::exec::StateClient class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td undefinedStateCallback td callback to be invoked by StateClient library if a FunctionGroup changes its state unexpectedly to an Undefined Function Group State, i.e. without previous request by SetState(). The affected FunctionGroup and ExecutionError is provided as an argument to the callback in form of ExecutionErrorEvent. Lifetime: it is expected that undefinedStateCallback remains callable, during entire lifetime of the StateClient instance. This is especially important if, undefinedStateCallback is bound to an instance of a class (e.g. using std::bind). Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; StateClient &gt; td a result that contains either a StateClient object or an error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td ara::exec::ExecErrc::kNoCommunication td no_rollback_semantics Communication error occurred. Recovery: try again td ara::exec::ExecErrc::kInvalidArgument td rollback_semantics Given undefinedStateCallback doesn’t contain a callable function. Recovery: change argument Hinweise: This named constructor may call a private constructor defined by the developer.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"c